From 4b9ea056867922688404a92227d2a2bd4407bae1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] elf_hook: detect 64-bit ELF by __LP64__, not just
 __x86_64

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted upstream from this session]

elf_hook.c picks the Elf64_* struct family only when __x86_64 is
defined, and falls back to Elf32_* for every other target - including
every other 64-bit architecture (aarch64, riscv64, ...). On a 64-bit
ELF shared object this misreads the section/symbol table layout
entirely (wrong struct sizes and field offsets), so elf_hook()'s
symbol lookup and PLT/GOT patch silently fail on anything but
x86_64. This matches the fact that greenify has never published a
wheel for any architecture other than x86_64 (confirmed via PyPI's
full release history), even though nothing else in the ELF-hook
implementation (the actual GOT/PLT relocation patch in elf_hook())
is architecture-specific - it only touches the GOT/PLT entry via the
generic ELF relocation mechanism, not an instruction encoding.

__LP64__ is defined by GCC/Clang on every LP64 target (x86_64,
aarch64, riscv64, ...), so this keeps x86_64's existing behaviour
and extends the 64-bit path to riscv64 without touching anything
else.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/elf_hook.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/elf_hook.c b/src/elf_hook.c
index 8c4dac1..2d30a93 100644
--- a/src/elf_hook.c
+++ b/src/elf_hook.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 //rename standart types for convenience
-#ifdef __x86_64
+#if defined(__x86_64) || defined(__LP64__)
     #define Elf_Ehdr Elf64_Ehdr
     #define Elf_Shdr Elf64_Shdr
     #define Elf_Sym Elf64_Sym
